## Data

- **Used:** `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` (Google Merchandise Store, {{ period }}: 903,653 sessions, 714,167 users). The SQL in `sql/` reduces it to user-level extracts in `data/processed/*.parquet`, which are committed. Extract totals reconcile exactly with the source.
- **Considered and rejected:** the REES46 e-commerce dataset (Kaggle). It has no traffic source, channel or campaign column, so it cannot say which channel acquired a user.
- **Excluded:** Google's internal staff traffic, which arrives as Referral with source `(direct)`. Left in, it would make Referral look like the best channel, with ROI of {{ referral_incl_roi }} instead of {{ referral_roi }}.

## Assumptions

The sample has no cost data, so **spend is assumed**. Every value is set in [`config/assumptions.yaml`](config/assumptions.yaml). To change one, edit it there and run `make all`. Nothing in the code needs to change.

